 ## Overview
-This method maintains a target frame rate in VTK volume rendering by dynamically adjusting the sampling distance per frame based on the allocated render time budget [S1]. It sets itself apart from static adaptive methods by using a global time-budgeting controller that distributes frame time among scene props, rather than local error metrics [S1].
+This method maintains a target frame rate in volume rendering by dynamically adjusting the sampling distance per frame based on an allocated render time budget [S1]. It differs from local error-driven adaptive methods by using a global time-budgeting controller that distributes frame time among scene objects rather than computing per-pixel error metrics [S1].
 
 ## How it works
